## What reactivation does

At the customer's request the agent makes an expired Cash Pickup pickup collectable again. The transfer returns to ready for pickup with the same Pickup Number, rate and amount. It is collectable from the day of the reactivation, and its reactivation count rises by one.

## Condition on the ledger

An expired pickup is not made collectable again until the transfer's ledger carries the reactivation fee charge numbered with that reactivation's number.

That reactivation's number is the transfer's reactivation count plus one. While the transfer's ledger carries no reactivation fee charge with that number, the expired pickup is not made collectable again.

## The tool

The tool is `reactivate_expired_pickup_d4e94bda`, an agent-side tool. The agent unlocks it and then calls it.

One call does all of the following:
- returns the expired Cash Pickup transfer to ready for pickup, with the same Pickup Number, rate and cash amount;
- makes it collectable from today;
- sets its last day of collection to today plus the window days given;
- clears its expiry date;
- raises its reactivation count by one.

The recipient can collect again from today with the same Pickup Number.

## Parameters

- `cash_transfer_id`: the reference number of the expired Cash Pickup transfer, as returned by the Cash Pickup transfer lookup for this customer. Identifier.
- `pickup_window_days`: the number of calendar days in the new pickup window, as a whole non-negative integer. The last day of collection becomes today's date plus this many days.

## Return

A successful call returns a receipt with these fields:
- `status`: "reactivated" when the transfer was made collectable;
- `transfer_status`: always `ready_for_pickup`;
- `available_date`: today;
- `pickup_expiry_date`: the new last day of collection;
- `reactivation_count`: the reactivations on the transfer, including this one;
- `pickup_reference`: the unchanged 10-digit Pickup Number.
